WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:14.908
"What?" Perda cried.

2
00:00:15.649 --> 00:00:17.530
She stared at the mysterious man.

3
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.772
"Morb is your brother?"

4
00:00:19.792 --> 00:00:23.254
"That's why you look familiar," Zann said.

5
00:00:23.274 --> 00:00:25.996
"You look kind of like him."

6
00:00:26.016 --> 00:00:27.917
"What were you saying about my brother?"

7
00:00:28.178 --> 00:00:28.998
the man demanded.

8
00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:31.240
Zann's heart pounded.

9
00:00:31.692 --> 00:00:34.773
What if Morb's brother was just as evil as Morb?

10
00:00:35.673 --> 00:00:38.234
What if Morb had sent him to capture the kids?

11
00:00:38.254 --> 00:00:41.515
"None of your business," Zann blurted out.

12
00:00:43.315 --> 00:00:48.277
He grabbed Darb with one hand and Gliss with the other, hoping that Perda saw what he was

13
00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:49.617
doing. "Zap!"

14
00:00:51.298 --> 00:00:56.819
Splash! They landed in a courtyard fountain just inside one of the palace entrances.

15
00:00:57.799 --> 00:00:59.480
Several guards hurried toward them.

16
00:01:00.652 --> 00:01:01.833
"Where did you kids zap from?"

17
00:01:02.053 --> 00:01:03.233
the biggest guard demanded.

18
00:01:03.253 --> 00:01:06.995
"The use of magic within palace walls is forbidden without permission!"

19
00:01:09.136 --> 00:01:10.536
Zann stepped out of the fountain.

20
00:01:10.556 --> 00:01:11.917
"Since when?"

21
00:01:11.937 --> 00:01:14.198
"Since yesterday."

22
00:01:14.498 --> 00:01:16.039
The guard narrowed his eyes.

23
00:01:16.059 --> 00:01:17.860
"Who are you anyway?

24
00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.720
You look familiar."

25
00:01:20.781 --> 00:01:22.301
"Nobody," Zann said quickly.

26
00:01:22.321 --> 00:01:24.322
"We were just trying to leave."

27
00:01:25.123 --> 00:01:27.984
The guard snapped his fingers, and the Directory appeared.

28
00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:31.261
A second later he was reading Zann's page.

29
00:01:31.281 --> 00:01:34.302
"Oh, I see," the guard said.

30
00:01:34.322 --> 00:01:36.842
"Your parents and grandfather are in the dungeon.

31
00:01:37.623 --> 00:01:39.403
Maybe we should take you there as well."

32
00:01:40.463 --> 00:01:41.284
Zann gulped.

33
00:01:41.724 --> 00:01:43.744
He tried to figure out how they could escape.

34
00:01:44.585 --> 00:01:47.606
At that moment Morb's brother zapped into view nearby.

35
00:01:47.626 --> 00:01:51.287
"It's all right," he told the guard in a stern voice.

36
00:01:51.307 --> 00:01:55.148
"These rascals slipped away from me, but it won't happen again."

37
00:01:56.192 --> 00:01:57.493
"They're with you, Maff?"

38
00:01:57.733 --> 00:01:59.315
The guard sounded surprised.

39
00:01:59.335 --> 00:02:02.818
"Yes. Laddno wishes to speak with them."

40
00:02:03.598 --> 00:02:05.200
Maff rubbed his hands together.

41
00:02:06.281 --> 00:02:08.583
Magical shackles appeared around the kids' arms.

42
00:02:08.603 --> 00:02:10.644
"Thanks for catching them for me."

43
00:02:11.585 --> 00:02:13.047
"Hey!" Perda cried.

44
00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:16.810
"But The guard sounded slightly suspicious.

45
00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:18.852
"That will be all, sir."

46
00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.413
Maff turned away.

47
00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:22.655
"Come, all four of you.

48
00:02:23.235 --> 00:02:23.836
It's this way."

49
00:02:24.996 --> 00:02:29.557
Zann didn't trust Morb's brother, but he didn't want to end up in the dungeon either.

50
00:02:30.337 --> 00:02:33.798
So he followed Maff out of the courtyard, pulling his friends along.

51
00:02:33.818 --> 00:02:37.839
"Are you sure this is a good idea?"

52
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:38.660
Perda whispered.

53
00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.240
"What if he's working with his brother?"

54
00:02:42.441 --> 00:02:43.901
Zann wondered the same thing.

55
00:02:43.921 --> 00:02:47.242
"Are you really taking us to see Laddno?"

56
00:02:47.442 --> 00:02:48.342
he asked Maff.

57
00:02:49.383 --> 00:02:50.543
Maff glanced at him.

58
00:02:50.563 --> 00:02:51.963
"Of course not.

59
00:02:52.563 --> 00:02:54.504
I hold no loyalty to that bully.

60
00:02:55.328 --> 00:02:57.750
He's as crooked as the Wormwood tree itself."

61
00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.552
"What do you mean?"

62
00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:00.372
Gliss said.

63
00:03:00.392 --> 00:03:02.774
"He's running for King of Magica."

64
00:03:03.615 --> 00:03:08.939
"Yes, and we can only hope that Venna crushes him in the election," Maff said grimly.

65
00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:13.423
"Who knows what Laddno has in mind for Magica if he's elected.

66
00:03:14.003 --> 00:03:21.289
His entire business empire is based on shady deals and black market goods, mostly from other worlds."

67
00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.712
"Really?" Perda's eyes widened.

68
00:03:25.612 --> 00:03:26.733
"How do you know that?"

69
00:03:26.753 --> 00:03:29.835
"I have my ways," Maff said.

70
00:03:29.855 --> 00:03:35.878
"I found out Laddno provided several of the items my brother used in his evil contraptions."

71
00:03:35.898 --> 00:03:40.961
"I thought Wyssa brought Morb all that stuff from other worlds," Zann said.

72
00:03:40.981 --> 00:03:44.063
"She brought most of it," Maff said.

73
00:03:44.083 --> 00:03:48.766
"But there were a few things that even she wasn't willing to help Morb with."

74
00:03:49.947 --> 00:03:51.668
"Wow." Zann was stunned.

75
00:03:52.288 --> 00:03:56.569
He hadn't paid much attention to Laddno, or worried much about the election either.

76
00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:00.971
But now it sounded as if Laddno was really bad news!

77
00:04:02.091 --> 00:04:05.472
Then again, how could he be sure that Maff was telling the truth?

78
00:04:06.092 --> 00:04:08.413
After all, he was Morb's brother.

79
00:04:14.215 --> 00:04:17.616
you're not taking us to Laddno, where are you taking us?"

80
00:04:17.956 --> 00:04:18.596
Darb asked.

81
00:04:19.532 --> 00:04:22.213
"Wherever the guards won't find you," Maff replied.

82
00:04:22.233 --> 00:04:26.915
"If they dump you in the dungeon, you won't be able to tell me why you were talking

83
00:04:26.955 --> 00:04:28.316
about my brother just now."

84
00:04:29.676 --> 00:04:31.537
Zann traded a look with his friends.

85
00:04:32.217 --> 00:04:33.318
Perda was frowning.

86
00:04:33.338 --> 00:04:38.160
"We're not going to tell you anything while you're holding us prisoner," she said.

87
00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:44.982
"What?" Maff blinked and then glanced at the magical shackles still holding the kids together.

88
00:04:45.002 --> 00:04:47.423
"Oh, the Shackle spell.

89
00:04:48.084 --> 00:04:51.197
Sorry, I only conjured that to trick those guards.

90
00:04:51.898 --> 00:04:54.779
If I release you, will you promise not to zap away again?"

91
00:04:54.799 --> 00:04:57.741
"We won't promise you anything!"

92
00:04:58.001 --> 00:04:58.641
Gliss cried.

93
00:04:59.762 --> 00:05:01.783
Maff grinned and snapped his fingers.

94
00:05:02.743 --> 00:05:05.785
Zann braced himself for some horrible new spell to hit them.

95
00:05:06.465 --> 00:05:08.226
Instead the shackles disappeared.

96
00:05:09.487 --> 00:05:11.488
Perda rubbed her arm where the shackles had been.

97
00:05:11.508 --> 00:05:15.010
"I thought you'd only release us if we talked."

98
00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:18.352
"I'm not my brother," Maff said.

99
00:05:18.824 --> 00:05:20.645
"I hope you'll tell me what I want to know.

100
00:05:21.425 --> 00:05:23.725
If not, I'll still help you escape."

101
00:05:23.745 --> 00:05:28.147
"Really?" Perda shot Zann an uncertain glance.

102
00:05:29.107 --> 00:05:30.607
Zann wasn't sure what to say.

103
00:05:31.068 --> 00:05:34.328
He was surprised that Maff had released them before getting what he wanted.

104
00:05:35.329 --> 00:05:37.309
That wasn't a very Morb-like thing to do.

105
00:05:38.069 --> 00:05:40.830
Maybe Maff wasn't much like his brother after all.

106
00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:42.731
"Come in here."

107
00:05:43.131 --> 00:05:44.851
Maff stepped into a nearby room.

108
00:05:44.871 --> 00:05:46.612
"We should stay out of sight."

109
00:05:47.804 --> 00:05:48.785
Zann hesitated.

110
00:05:49.565 --> 00:05:52.407
Then he shrugged and followed Maff into the room.

111
00:05:52.427 --> 00:05:55.710
"We might as well trust him," he told his friends.

112
00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.792
"Maybe he can help us free my parents and the others."

113
00:05:58.812 --> 00:06:02.895
"Okay." Perda still sounded uncertain.

114
00:06:02.915 --> 00:06:06.978
"So should we tell him about, you know, Morb?"

115
00:06:06.998 --> 00:06:10.040
"Please do," Maff urged.

116
00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.081
"Then I'll tell you what I know."

117
00:06:12.101 --> 00:06:15.564
"Okay." Zann took a deep breath.

118
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.001
"It started several days ago.

119
00:06:18.362 --> 00:06:23.666
I thought I was receiving a Red Share He went on to tell Maff the whole story, with

120
00:06:23.706 --> 00:06:25.227
his friends chiming in now and then.

121
00:06:26.288 --> 00:06:28.490
Maff looked more and more alarmed.

122
00:06:29.071 --> 00:06:33.554
When he heard that Morb seemed to have magic power again, his eyes widened.

123
00:06:34.855 --> 00:06:40.901
And when the kids described how Morb had grabbed the guidelink and disappeared into the vortex, Maff went

124
00:06:41.021 --> 00:06:43.763
pale. "This is terrible!"

125
00:06:44.043 --> 00:06:44.764
Maff exclaimed.

126
00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.723
"We didn't mean to release Morb," Gliss said.

127
00:06:48.743 --> 00:06:51.645
"He tricked us," Perda added.

128
00:06:51.665 --> 00:06:53.106
"I know."

129
00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:55.008
Maff nodded wearily.

130
00:06:55.028 --> 00:06:57.450
"You kids shouldn't blame yourselves.

131
00:06:58.171 --> 00:06:59.492
This is all my fault!"
